---
description: SvelteKit and Svelte 5 coding conventions for this project
globs: "**/*.svelte,**/*.ts,**/*.js"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Use Svelte 5 runes only. No legacy `$:` reactive statements or `export let`.
- Use `<script lang="ts">`, `$props()`, `$state`, `$derived`, and `$effect`.
- Keep browser-only APIs out of server files such as `+page.server.ts`, `+layout.server.ts`, `+server.ts`, and `src/lib/server/**`.
- Prefer SvelteKit load functions and form actions over client fetch when the flow fits the framework.
- Test user-visible behavior with Vitest and Svelte Testing Library using accessible queries.
- Read `.claude/conventions/svelte-style.md` for the full guide.
